From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:25:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qcow2: join thread and clean on failed open.

A failed open never joined the thread. Tapdisk frees the driver state
and retries the open, so a retry can re-initialize the QEMU globals
(BQL, main loop, AIO context, signal fd) while the previous thread is
still destroying them, and every failed open leaks a joinable thread.
Join before returning the error.

Signed-off-by: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/block-qcow2.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/block-qcow2.c b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
index 43fc3c7d..6b5a3da4 100644
--- a/drivers/block-qcow2.c
+++ b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
@@ -570,6 +570,19 @@ _qcow2_open(td_driver_t *driver, const char *name,
 	s->open_status = 0;
 	pthread_mutex_unlock(&s->lock);
 
+	if (err) {
+		/*
+                 * Join the teardown thread before returning so a retried
+                 * open doesn't reinit QEMU globals while it's still running.
+		 */
+		qemu_thread_join(&s->thread);
+
+		pthread_cond_destroy(&s->commit_cond);
+		pthread_mutex_destroy(&s->commit_lock);
+		pthread_cond_destroy(&s->cond);
+		pthread_mutex_destroy(&s->lock);
+	}
+
 	return err;
 }
 
